# Original ledger observation decoder

Import AlejandroJsonFields from "./alejandro_json_fields.lg".
Import AlejandroLedgerRow from "./alejandro_ledger_row.lg".
Import AlejandroProvenance from "./alejandro_provenance.lg".

## An AlejandroLedger has:
    a caseId, which is Text.
    a declarationCount, which is Int.
    a rawDigest, which is Text.
    a recorded, which is Json.
## To decodeAlejandroLedgerObject (object: Json, expectedCase: Text, digest: Text) -> Result of AlejandroLedger and Text:
    Inspect jsonNoExtraKeys(object, ["case", "lean", "lean_compiles", "declarations"]):
        When Ok (accepted): Let _ be accepted.
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
    Repeat for key in ["case", "lean"]:
        Inspect alejandroStringField(object, key):
            When Err (failure):
                Return a new Err with error failure.
            When Ok (value):
                If key is equal to "case" and value is not equal to expectedCase:
                    Return a new Err with error "ledger belongs to another case".
                If key is equal to "lean" and value is not equal to "4.14.0":
                    Return a new Err with error "ledger reports another Lean release".
    Inspect jsonField(object, "lean_compiles"):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
        When Ok (field):
            Inspect jsonBool(field):
                When Ok (accepted): Let _ be accepted.
                When Err (failure):
                    Return a new Err with error failure.
    Let mutable rows be a new Seq of Json.
    Inspect alejandroArrayField(object, "declarations"):
        When Ok (items):
            Set rows to items.
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
    Let seen be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for row in rows:
        Inspect validateAlejandroDeclaration(row):
            When Err (failure):
                Return a new Err with error failure.
            When Ok (name):
                Repeat for previous in seen:
                    If previous is equal to name:
                        Return a new Err with error "duplicate recorded declaration".
                Push name to seen.
    Let observation be a new AlejandroLedger with caseId expectedCase and declarationCount (length of rows) and rawDigest digest and recorded object.
    Return a new Ok with value observation.
## To decodeAlejandroLedger (raw: Text, expectedCase: Text) -> Result of AlejandroLedger and Text:
    Inspect alejandroStrictObject(raw):
        When Err (failure):
            Return a new Err with error failure.
        When Ok (object):
            Return decodeAlejandroLedgerObject(object, expectedCase, alejandroRawDigest(raw)).
    Return a new Err with error "invalid recorded ledger".
